 "id": "c2",
 "title": "The two channels and the middle cell, by hand",
 "why": "Between the GND busbar and the middle cell both outer layers are battery pour, except under the FET bodies: 2.8 mm between each FET's source pads and its drain tab (x 136.85-139.65 west, 170.35-173.15 east). The bulk router ignored these and cut the pours. Seven lines go down the west channel and four down the east at 0.3 mm pitch on B.Cu; the cell under the VBAT_IN bar is B.Cu only, so its lines arrive in pin order. Four plane vias go so RS_SENSE_N can run straight north beside the shunt's sense pad: three of VBAT_D at x 160.05 (y 83.7, 84.6, 85.5) and one of VBAT_Q2D at (159.85, 88.15). The lanes' north ends are staggered 0.5 mm, the east-most lowest, so each line can turn east in turn.",
